    "title": "Tennessee Titans awarded offensive tackle Brant Banks off waivers - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Mark Mihalko ,\n2 hours ago Green Bay Packers offensive tackle Brant Banks (72) is shown during a joint practice with the Seattle Seahawks Thursday, August 21, 2025 in Green Bay, Wisconsin. By Mark Hoffman/Milwaukee Journal Sentinel, Mark Hoffman/Milwaukee Journal Sentinel / USA TODAY NETWORK via Imagn Images The Tennessee Titans continue to utilize their placement on the waiver wire to help manage their roster, and on Wednesday, they were awarded offensive tackle Brant Banks off waivers from the Green Bay Packers .\nThe 6-foot-7, 306-pound Banks entered the league with the Packers as an undrafted rookie free agent out of Rice following the 2025 NFL draft.\nBanks opened the season on the Packers' practice squad, but was signed to the active 53-man roster ahead of their Week 4 battle with the Dallas Cowboys. In all, he has seen action in two games during the season and has logged multiple special teams snaps.\nBanks was then caught up in a numbers game, with the Packers getting healthy along the offensive line and preparing to activate multiple players to the active roster.\nThe Titans will return to the field on Thursday, as they continue preparations for their Week 5 matchup with the Arizona Cardinals.\nThis article originally appeared on Titans Wire: Tennessee Titans awarded offensive tackle Brant Banks off waivers",
